From b710163720f29c7522273585438933690700ce80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 10:51:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: graph_optimize no longer hoists a UNARY away from the
 MUL it fuses with (W1 collision V023)

On the union the Qwen3.8 GDN layers lost upstream's SILU+MUL fusion (vanilla b11178 48 SILU_MUL per graph, union 0; with GGML_VK_DISABLE_GRAPH_OPTIMIZE=1 both fuse 48). Cause, traced with an uncommitted order dump (cache/lane296/trace-u7.patch, trace-v.patch): the fork's GDN node order lets the reorder pull MUL_MAT z ahead of GATED_DELTA_NET, then silu(z) follows it, while the gate MUL needs the RMS_NORM output and cannot; the pair splits. Vanilla keeps the pair only by node-order luck. The fork's F-136 is_src_of clauses never fire on these pairs. Fix: a fusable UNARY is not hoisted while its MUL partner's other operand is still pending. It only removes reorders, so it cannot re-open the F-136 read/write hazard.

Measured-effect: none claimed; fused-op census + quality regate in lane-296 run 13
Lane: lane-296
---
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
index 579b30def5..f0b35e574b 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
@@ -17248,6 +17248,24 @@ void ggml_vk_graph_optimize(ggml_backend_t backend, struct ggml_cgraph * graph,
                 match_pattern(rope_view_set_rows_pattern, j)) {
                 continue;
             }
+            // ARIFI lane-296 V023: never hoist a UNARY away from the MUL it fuses with while that MUL's
+            // other operand is still pending - the MUL cannot follow, so the pair splits and the fusion is lost.
+            if (graph->nodes[j]->op == GGML_OP_UNARY && ggml_vk_unary_mul_op_index(ggml_get_unary_op(graph->nodes[j])) >= 0) {
+                bool strands_mul = false;
+                for (int k = j + 1; k < std::min(j + 15, graph->n_nodes); ++k) {
+                    ggml_tensor * mul = graph->nodes[k];
+                    if (mul->op != GGML_OP_MUL || (mul->src[0] != graph->nodes[j] && mul->src[1] != graph->nodes[j])) {
+                        continue;
+                    }
+                    ggml_tensor * other = (mul->src[0] == graph->nodes[j]) ? mul->src[1] : mul->src[0];
+                    strands_mul = ggml_vk_can_fuse_unary_mul(graph, j, k) &&
+                                  !(other->op == GGML_OP_NONE || used_node_set.find(other) != used_node_set.end());
+                    break;
+                }
+                if (strands_mul) {
+                    continue;
+                }
+            }
             bool ok = true;
             for (int c = first_unused; c < j; ++c) {
                 if (!used[c] &&
